    "closedB": {
      "type": "number",
      "attribute": true,
      "default": 0,
      "min": 0,
      "max": 1,
      "step": 1,
      "label": "End B closed",
      "group": "State",
      "desc": "1 puts a floor across the +Z end. A machine sets this with End B fold stage 6."
    },
    "foldA": {
      "type": "number",
      "attribute": true,
      "default": 0,
      "min": 0,
      "max": 6,
      "step": 1,
      "label": "End A fold stage",
      "group": "State",
      "desc": "The flaps at the -Z end. 0 has them standing straight out, 1 to 3 fold the short end flaps in (30 degrees a stage), 4 to 6 the long side flaps. 6 is a closed end, and a flat sleeve has its flaps folded flat."
    },
    "foldB": {
      "type": "number",
      "attribute": true,
      "default": 0,
      "min": 0,
      "max": 6,
      "step": 1,
      "label": "End B fold stage",
      "group": "State",
      "desc": "The flaps at the +Z end, as End A fold stage."
    },
    "tapedA": {
      "type": "number",
      "attribute": true,
      "default": 0,
      "min": 0,
      "max": 1,
      "step": 1,
      "label": "End A taped",
      "group": "State",
      "desc": "1 puts a strip of tape down the seam at the -Z end."
    },
    "tapedB": {
      "type": "number",
      "attribute": true,
      "default": 0,
      "min": 0,
      "max": 1,
      "step": 1,
      "label": "End B taped",
      "group": "State",
      "desc": "1 puts a strip of tape down the seam at the +Z end."
    }
  },
  "behavior": "// Carton: a corrugated shipping case that folds, cargo with its own body (docs/cargo-bodies.md). It is a four-walled\n// tube with a set of four flaps at each end, and a machine takes it from a flat blank to a taped case with ctx.reform:\n//   - a flat blank, as it lies in the magazine: a sleeve pressed flat, `open` 0, with the flaps at both ends folded flat;\n//   - a tube opening: `open` grows from 0 to 1 and the section goes from flat to a parallelogram to a rectangle, the\n//     walls hinged at their corners, as the robot lifts the blank by one face;\n//   - an erected tube: `open` 1, the flaps at both ends standing straight out;\n//   - one end's flaps closing, `foldA` or `foldB`, 1 to 6: the short end flaps fold in first (stages 1 to 3, 30 degrees\n//     each) and the long side flaps after (4 to 6);\n//   - one end taped: `tapedA` or `tapedB`, a strip of tape down the seam of that end.\n// The two ends are the tube's -Z end (A) and +Z end (B), each with its own state, so a case closes and tapes one end and\n// is turned over to do the other, or is filled through the open end between the two.\n//\n// The tube runs along the part's Z, its section is Length (X) by Width (Y) and Height is the way it runs. So a blank is\n// born lying flat, thin in Y, and the robot stands the case up (Z to world up) when it wants it open end up.\n//\n// The collider is hollow, so the case can be filled: four walls 10 mm thick, whose spacing follows `open` (flat, they lie one\n// on the other), two wings that make a flat sleeve as wide as it is, and a floor across an end once that end is closed\n// (`closedA`, `closedB`). An open end has no floor, so a product dropped in at the open end stays in the case and one\n// dropped in at a closed end does not. What is drawn is the walls, the flaps and the tape, all with collision off. The\n// walls hinge on frame links whose rotation follows `open`, and each flap hinges on its wall's edge, so the folding is the\n// rig's `rotationParams` and not a joint (a rigid cargo body has none).\n//\n// `open`, `flat`, the folds and the tapes change the look but not the collider (apart from opening and closing), so they are\n// `visualParams`: the sim and view give each combination its own batch. The state is a product attribute too, so a beam\n// that hits a case reads it off its marks, which is how a folding rig knows what is left to do. `flat` is `1 - open`, kept\n// as its own param because the wings need a product with it. A machine that changes one changes the other.\n//\n// Nothing here is simulated, so step() is empty.\n//\n// This is the part's source. `npm run build-parts` writes behavior.ts and rig.json from it.\n\n// The default case, 0.4 x 0.3 x 0.25. Every number that follows a param carries its ref, spelled out: the build fits a\n// ref to a plain linear param, not a product that is clamped, and it cannot fit a rotation to a param at all.\nconst L = 0.4\nconst W = 0.3\nconst H = 0.25\n\ndefinePart({\n  params: {\n    length: { type: 'number', attribute: true, default: L, min: 0.1, max: 1.2, step: 0.005, label: 'Length (m)', group: 'Size', desc: 'The tube section along X. Keep it at least as long as the width: the long flaps close over the short ones.' },\n    width: { type: 'number', attribute: true, default: W, min: 0.1, max: 1, step: 0.005, label: 'Width (m)', group: 'Size', desc: 'The tube section along Y. This is also how deep each flap is, half of it.' },\n    height: { type: 'number', attribute: true, default: H, min: 0.05, max: 1, step: 0.005, label: 'Height (m)', group: 'Size', desc: 'The way the tube runs, along Z: the case stands this tall once the robot sets it upright.' },\n    mass: { type: 'number', default: 1.5, min: 0.1, max: 60, step: 0.1, label: 'Mass (kg)', desc: 'Physical mass.' },\n    color: { type: 'color', default: '#b98b57', label: 'Color', desc: 'The board. Kraft brown by default.' },\n    open: { type: 'number', attribute: true, default: 1, min: 0, max: 1, step: 0.05, label: 'Open', group: 'State', desc: '0 is a flat sleeve and 1 a rectangular tube. Between, the section is a parallelogram. A machine sets this together with Flat.' },\n    flat: { type: 'number', default: 0, min: 0, max: 1, step: 0.05, label: 'Flat', group: 'State', desc: '1 minus Open. Set it together with Open.' },\n    closedA: { type: 'number', attribute: true, default: 0, min: 0, max: 1, step: 1, label: 'End A closed', group: 'State', desc: '1 puts a floor across the -Z end: what an end with its flaps shut is, to anything set in the case. A machine sets this with End A fold stage 6.' },\n    closedB: { type: 'number', attribute: true, default: 0, min: 0, max: 1, step: 1, label: 'End B closed', group: 'State', desc: '1 puts a floor across the +Z end. A machine sets this with End B fold stage 6.' },\n    foldA: { type: 'number', attribute: true, default: 0, min: 0, max: 6, step: 1, label: 'End A fold stage', group: 'State', desc: 'The flaps at the -Z end. 0 has them standing straight out, 1 to 3 fold the short end flaps in (30 degrees a stage), 4 to 6 the long side flaps. 6 is a closed end, and a flat sleeve has its flaps folded flat.' },\n    foldB: { type: 'number', attribute: true, default: 0, min: 0, max: 6, step: 1, label: 'End B fold stage', group: 'State', desc: 'The flaps at the +Z end, as End A fold stage.' },\n    tapedA: { type: 'number', attribute: true, default: 0, min: 0, max: 1, step: 1, label: 'End A taped', group: 'State', desc: '1 puts a strip of tape down the seam at the -Z end.' },\n    tapedB: { type: 'number', attribute: true, default: 0, min: 0, max: 1, step: 1, label: 'End B taped', group: 'State', desc: '1 puts a strip of tape down the seam at the +Z end.' },\n  },\n  step() {},\n})\n",
